            "review_title": "Review at Ngon Pho",
            "review_text": "Sonny_Foodie\nFreehold, New Jersey159 contributions\n0\nTerrible food, Service was average\nJul 2017 • Friends\nFood was very salty and almost inedible, server did not take the order properly. Ordered orange Fanta for a drink, checked first if they have it, said no problem, and brought out Minute Maid orange drink, when asked why the substitute said it tastes same as you ordered. I opened the can and it tasted like flat orange flavored dish water, I said take this away it tastes terrible, the server argued that because you opened it, he has to charge for it. I paid for it, along with the overpriced meal and wrote it off to another crappy experience at the mall. The servers look like they are high school kids with next to no training. The restaurant takes up a very large area of the food court and is never busy, that should be a hint to the management, train your servers better, deliver better quality food and a reasonable price and you will get more customers.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 31, 2017\nNgon Garden HN\nDear Sonny_Foodie\n\nThanks so much for your review. Your feedback is so helpful in knowing what we're doing and where we should improve. Please accept our apologies for the service you received the other day. It sounds like your server was having an off day, as the behavior you're describing is not the norm for anyone on our team. And maybe language barrier made him couldn't understand exactly everything you said. We make sure to follow bring it up and never let it doesn't happen again. It's understandable that you left disappointed, but We hope you will give us another opportunity as we'd love to have you as our customers again!\n\nBest regards,\nNgon Pho Restaurants\nRead more\nWritten August 1, 2017\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
